# Preserve the immutable reference package's recorded bytes on every platform.
docs/reference/phase2-package/** -text

# Digest-bound contract records must also survive an ordinary Windows checkout
# unchanged (#234).
#
# Every file named by a SHA-256 recorded in this repository is provenance
# evidence: the recorded digest is a claim about *exact* bytes, taken from the
# committed blob. `core.autocrlf=true` -- the Git for Windows default -- would
# otherwise rewrite LF to CRLF in the working tree for every file Git treats as
# text, so the digest of the working-tree bytes would necessarily stop matching
# a digest taken from LF bytes. That is what broke
# `node tools/verify-contract-pins.mjs` on a plain Windows clone.
#
# `-text` (rather than `text eol=lf`) is deliberate. It means Git performs no
# conversion in either direction, for these paths, on any platform, so the
# working tree always holds exactly the committed bytes. That is the property
# the digests depend on, and it holds no matter how a blob was committed.
# `text eol=lf` would keep the working tree LF for an LF-committed blob, but it
# only holds because of an assumption about how each blob was committed, and
# applying `text` to a directory would also mark its binary members for
# conversion.
#
# The consequence is intentionally fail-closed: a contributor who edits one of
# these files on Windows and commits will commit CRLF bytes, and
# `tools/verify-contract-pins.mjs` will report a digest mismatch rather than
# silently accept a converted artifact. Changing a pinned contract is a
# deliberate act that must re-pin the digest deliberately.
#
# `tools/audit-digest-bound.mjs` enforces this: it enumerates every tracked
# file pinned by a digest anywhere in the repository and fails if Git's
# effective attributes would expose any of them to line-ending conversion, so
# a newly pinned file cannot be added without coverage.

# Accepted contract artifacts: schemas, fixtures and the Phase 1 inventory.
contracts/accepted/** -text

# The recorded-run candidate contracts, including their SHA256SUMS inventory.
contracts/recorded-run-candidate/** -text

# The archived second recorded-run candidate contracts.
history/recorded-run-candidate2/contracts/** -text

# The bundle artifacts whose bytes docs/evidence/studio-bundle.SHA256SUMS pins.
# Scoped to these three files rather than all of docs/evidence/, because the
# ledgers and reports beside the inventory are not digest-bound.
artifacts/studio-bundle/** -text
docs/evidence/studio-bundle.SHA256SUMS -text

# The rule file is itself read by Git on every platform, so it must never be
# rewritten: a CRLF-terminated rule is silently ignored by Git.
.gitattributes -text
